[0.1.3]
* Cloudron single sign-on: the `oidc` addon is wired to Orbit's OpenID Connect sign-in, so Cloudron users can choose "Continue with Cloudron" on the sign-in page. Password and passkey sign-in are unchanged. A first SSO sign-in links to an existing Orbit account only when Cloudron reports the email as verified.

[0.1.2]
* Update to Orbit 0.4.1 (upstream commit 17ed06a): milestones, cycles and estimates, recurring tasks, private projects, custom workspace roles, task webhooks, `#` task references and ⌘K search (0.4.0), plus 0.4.1's write-lock and S3 reliability fixes.
* Orbit 0.4 can sign in with an OpenID Connect provider, but this package does not configure it yet, so Cloudron single sign-on is still not available.

[0.1.1]
* Update to Orbit 0.3.0 (upstream commit a740220): Notion-style databases in Docs, Orbit-to-Orbit import, a chat-only guest role, more MCP tools and Tasks/Docs trash controls.

[0.1.0]
* Initial Cloudron package for Orbit 0.2.1 (upstream commit fe9dce7), built from upstream's release image pinned by digest.
* SQLite database, attachments and the app key in /app/data, with Cloudron's consistent SQLite backups.
* Outgoing mail through the Cloudron relay: `orbit-mail-settings` prints the values for Admin → Email.
* `orbit-setup-link` prints a fresh first-run setup link; `orbit-offline` runs the upstream CLI commands that need the server stopped.
* Orbit's Mail section is still a preview with mock data upstream.
